<title>BELGIUM: EU, east Europe farm ministers to meet in March.</title>
<headline>EU, east Europe farm ministers to meet in March.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers will hold a third meeting with their east European counterparts in March to prepare for the EU's expansion east, an EU official said.</p>
<p>Senior EU member state agricultural officials decided on Monday that the next joint meeting would discuss how to make east European veterinary and plant health standards compatible with those in the EU, the official added.</p>
<p>No date was fixed, but officials noted that the incoming Dutch EU presidency had scheduled a Farm Council for April 17-19.</p>
<p>At their last joint meeting on June 25, farm ministers from the two sides discussed how to make farmers more competitive and ways to develop rural areas.</p>
<p>Poland, Hungary, the Czech Republic, Slovakia, Romania, Bulgaria, Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Slovenia have applied to join the EU, with the first candidates expected to enter early next century.</p>
</text>
